# Nothing here is needed to build or run the app, and all of it was
# being uploaded on every deployment.
#
# `docs/` alone is the bulk of it: design handoffs, research reports and
# the screen captures those reports cite. Reference material for the
# people building the product, not an input to the build.
#
# THAT CAVEAT RESOLVED — THIS FILE IS NOW THE DORMANT ONE.
#
# It used to end on an open question: "if Vercel's project root is ever
# set to `apps/web` rather than the repository root, this file stops
# applying." The root IS `apps/web` now, deliberately. `apps/web` is a
# self-contained Next.js project with its own package.json and its own
# pnpm lockfile; pointing Vercel at the repository root would aim it at
# `gsa-startup-kit`, the agent kit, which is not the product.
# See docs/03-system-design/RUNBOOK-deploy-vercel.md §2.
#
# So Vercel reads `apps/web/.vercelignore`, not this file. Every path
# below is already outside `apps/web` and therefore already outside the
# upload — this file changes nothing under the current configuration.
# It is kept because it stays correct for the other case (anyone who
# moves the root back gets these exclusions again), and because
# deleting it would delete the record of why the root is where it is.
docs/
war-room/
war-room-dashboard/
guides/

# Committed screen captures at the repository root, from earlier builds.
*.png
*.jpeg

.agent/
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
